NAME
    basicc - the BASIC interpreter, the C build (the same as basic)

SYNOPSIS
    basicc
    basicc file
    basicc -r file

DESCRIPTION
    The same program as basic: the same command line, statements,
    functions, messages, limits and files (man basic). basic is the
    interpreter written in YACC1 assembly (os/commands-asm/basic.asm,
    2026-11-11); basicc is os/commands/basic.c compiled by the C
    compiler, the specification basic.asm was written from. Both are
    kept in step: any change of behaviour goes into both, and
    tests/ybasic checks that they print and write the same, session
    by session.

    basicc needs about six times the instructions of basic for a
    program line, and is twice its size (14.5 K against 7.5 K).

SEE ALSO
    basic, asmc
